# Per-client topic ACL for ha-pellmon on the Home Assistant Mosquitto
# add-on. The add-on loads extra config through its "customize" option:
#
#   1. Add-on → Configuration → customize: { active: true, folder: mosquitto }
#   2. Create /share/mosquitto/acl.conf containing one line:
#        acl_file /share/mosquitto/accesscontrollist
#   3. Copy this file to /share/mosquitto/accesscontrollist
#   4. Restart the add-on.
#
# Least privilege: the compromise of one credential must not grant more
# than that client's role.
#
# CAUTION with wildcards: `pellmon/#` INCLUDES `pellmon/set/#`. The
# bridge therefore gets only single-level `pellmon/+` for states —
# never the multi-level wildcard — so a stolen bridge credential
# cannot publish commands.
#
# User names must match MQTT_USERNAME in .env (bridge) and the HA
# add-on's own login for Home Assistant.

# ── The bridge (MQTT_USERNAME) ──
# Publishes states, availability, results, and discovery; reads commands.
user pellmon-bridge
topic write pellmon/+
topic write pellmon/bridge/availability
topic read  pellmon/set/+
topic write pellmon/set/+/result
topic write homeassistant/sensor/+/config
topic write homeassistant/number/+/config
topic write homeassistant/select/+/config
topic write homeassistant/button/+/config
topic read  homeassistant/status

# ── Home Assistant ──
# Reads everything under pellmon/, writes commands ONLY (not results).
user homeassistant
topic read  pellmon/#
topic write pellmon/set/+
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

# No other user has any access to pellmon/# — do not add pattern rules.
